From a808693f375c9de59123ea0ac3ee39d7bdbbab6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Kovalov <artem.kovalyov@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:28:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] pgtk: map GDK_MOD3_MASK to hyper modifier
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CapsLock mapped to Hyper_L on Mod3 in XKB sends GDK_MOD3_MASK on
Wayland/pgtk, but this mask was not handled — the Hyper modifier was
silently dropped. GDK_HYPER_MASK is only set when GDK itself recognises
the keysym as Hyper, which doesn't happen reliably on all compositors.

Map GDK_MOD3_MASK → mod_hyper so CapsLock-based Hyper bindings work.
---
 src/pgtkterm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/pgtkterm.c b/src/pgtkterm.c
index a5d8c0f..b24d42b 100644
--- a/src/pgtkterm.c
+++ b/src/pgtkterm.c
@@ -5132,6 +5132,8 @@ pgtk_gtk_to_emacs_modifiers (struct pgtk_display_info *dpyinfo, int state)
     mod |= mod_alt;
   if (state & GDK_MOD2_MASK)
     mod |= mod_meta;
+  if (state & GDK_MOD3_MASK)
+    mod |= mod_hyper;
   if (state & GDK_SUPER_MASK)
     mod |= mod_super;
   if (state & GDK_HYPER_MASK)
